# Comprehensive Validations Across All Input and Edit Modals

All input (creation) and edit modals across the entire application—along with their corresponding backend API endpoints—have been enhanced with real-time validation, duplicate detection, boundary constraints, visual cues (`is-invalid` / `is-valid`), loading states, and async submission error handling.

---

## Modals Enhanced & Key Validations

### 1. Sites Module
- **[AddSiteModal.jsx](file:///d:/Chris/Web-Based-Construction-Labor-Management-System/Frontend/src/components/sites/AddSiteModal.jsx)**
  - **Site Name**: Required, 3–100 characters, uniqueness check against all existing sites.
  - **Project Code**: Format check (`3-30` chars, alphanumeric/hyphen/slash), uniqueness check if manually entered (or auto-generates).
  - **Location & Client**: Required, minimum character boundaries.
  - **Dates**: Commencement date required; completion date must be on or after commencement date.
  - **Budget**: Must be a positive number greater than 0; upper ceiling capped at Rs. 100 Billion.
  - **UX**: Asynchronous `isSubmitting` state with loading spinner, disabled inputs/buttons, error banner displaying backend rejection reasons without losing form inputs.
- **[EditSiteModal.jsx](file:///d:/Chris/Web-Based-Construction-Labor-Management-System/Frontend/src/components/sites/EditSiteModal.jsx)**
  - Full inline error message displays with `<AlertCircle />` added for all fields (`name`, `location`, `client`, `startDate`, `endDate`, `budget`, `manager`).
  - Duplicate site name validation against other sites (`id !== site.id`).
  - Budget & date range boundary enforcement.
  - Asynchronous submission handling and server error banner.
- **[SiteAllocationModal.jsx](file:///d:/Chris/Web-Based-Construction-Labor-Management-System/Frontend/src/components/sites/SiteAllocationModal.jsx)**
  - Displays count of reallocated workers when moving workers from another active site.
  - Asynchronous saving state (`isSaving` with spinner) and error alert banner.
- **[Backend/src/routes/sites.js](file:///d:/Chris/Web-Based-Construction-Labor-Management-System/Backend/src/routes/sites.js)**
  - Added backend checks for site name length and uniqueness on `POST /` and `PUT /:id`.
  - Added date consistency checks (`endDate >= startDate`) and non-negative budget enforcement.

